infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The forced choice when a partition splits the nodes
  desc During a network partition you cannot have both — you must sacrifice one
  compares
    - label Choose consistency
      children
        - label Refuse stale reads
          desc Isolated nodes stop answering until the network heals
        - label All nodes agree or none reply
          desc A user never reads contradictory data
        - label Cost paid
          desc Availability — some requests get no response
    - label Choose availability
      children
        - label Always return a response
          desc Even the isolated group keeps serving requests
        - label May serve stale data
          desc The answer can be out of date until nodes reconverge
        - label Cost paid
          desc Consistency — reads can disagree across nodes
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
